><td>81.51</td><td>85.20</td><td class="na">n/a</td><td class="na">n/a</td><td>0.7018</td></tr><tr><td>Jul 29</td><td>35,333.78</td><td>84.46</td><td>88.30</td><td class="na">n/a</td><td>3.20</td><td>0.7005</td></tr><tr><td>Jul 30</td><td>35,505.84</td><td>83.90</td><td>87.70</td><td>4,115</td><td class="na">n/a</td><td>0.7010</td></tr><tr><td>Jul 31</td><td>35,226.14</td><td>85.47</td><td>89.20</td><td>4,145</td><td>3.26</td><td>0.7015</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="font-size:11px;color:#666;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">*July 22 TSX close of 35,626 stands three points below the June 17 intraday all-time high of 35,629. July 1 (Canada Day) was a full market holiday and is not shown above.</p>',
